    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Buckle Up,\" released in September 2025 on Decca Records, is Adam Buxton's debut studio album, blending electronic music with elements of spoken word, comedy sketches, and quirky jingles. Over 15 tracks and about 33 minutes, the album presents a collage of observational humor and self-aware, lightly produced soundscapes, largely crafted with the help of Metronomy’s Joseph Mount. The musical style is deliberately unpolished yet surprisingly slick, mixing deadpan vocal delivery with playful, often absurd lyrical content about everyday life, such as culinary mishaps and modern anxieties.\n\nPositioned as a unique entry in Buxton’s career, \"Buckle Up\" builds on his long-standing reputation as a comedian and podcaster known for musical interludes and humorous jingles. Unlike traditional albums, it functions more like a comedy sketch show in audio form, reflecting Buxton’s podcast-era creativity rather than aiming for timeless musical acclaim. Critics have noted its charm and niche appeal, highlighting tracks like \"Shorts\" and \"My Feelings\" for their genuine moments amid the silliness. While some find the album disposable on first listen, it is appreciated as a personal and entertaining detour rather than a conventional musical statement.",
